(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "adr-2607171600-docs-adr-edn-only-datascript"), (:adr/title "ADR-2607171600: docs/ADR は kotoba のみ — DataScript/datom query が正経路（2026-09-10 訂正: 形式は edn から kotoba へ動いた。datom query の決定は不変）"), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/topic "docs-edn-only"), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-09-10"), (:adr/source-format "kotoba"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "90-docs EDN-only SSoT" "DataScript query path" "docs-edn-only verify" "BMC .edn projections")), (:adr/related (vector "manifest/edn-datomize.cljs" "manifest/edn-query.cljs" "manifest/docs-edn-only.cljs" "manifest/schema.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607021500-portfolio-bmc-lean.datoms.edn")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/problem "docs/ADR が md と edn の二重管理になり DataScript 横断 query ができない。md を正本とみなし edn を投影扱いする運用は再発の温床。"), (:adr/decision "90-docs/adr の正本は .kotoba のみ。md は正本でも生成物でもない。最初から kotoba の S 式 tx-data を書く。⚠ 90-docs 全体は kotoba only ではない —— datom catalog と ledger は .edn のまま残り、gate docs-edn-check は両方を受ける。"), (:adr/consequences (vector "90-docs/adr に .md を置かない" "ADR は .kotoba で読み書き" "横断検索は datalog" "source-format は kotoba" "datom catalog と ledger は .edn のまま" "scripts/adr-new.cljs は .edn と bare id を出すので直してから commit する")), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607171600: docs/ADR は kotoba のみ — DataScript/datom query が正経路\n\n## Status\naccepted — 2026-07-17、形式は 2026-09-10 に訂正（下の Correction 節）\n\n## Decision (normative)\n1. EDN is the sole SSoT for 90-docs/ (especially adr/). No .md files.\n2. Do not treat EDN as a projection of markdown. Author EDN tx-data from day one.\n3. Shape: [{:db/id -1 :adr/id ...}].\n4. Nested maps/vectors: pr-str string blobs.\n5. Query: kbb --backend sci --classpath \".:scripts/nbb_compat\" manifest/edn-query.cljs\n6. Verify: kbb --backend sci --classpath \".:scripts/nbb_compat\" manifest/docs-edn-only.cljs verify\n7. BMC projections write .edn only.\n8. Multi-entity *.datoms.edn catalogs stay multi-entity.\n\n## Correction, 2026-09-10\n\nItem 1 said EDN. The tree moved to `.kotoba` and this ADR did not, so the\nrule kept pointing at a format the ADR plane no longer uses -- **including\nthis file, which is itself a .kotoba document asserting EDN-only.**\n\nMeasured 2026-09-10 on origin/main:\n\n    90-docs/adr   2,884 .kotoba   1 .json   0 .edn\n    90-docs total 2,907 .kotoba   617 .edn  88 .md\n\nSo the correction is narrow and must stay narrow. **The ADR plane is\nkotoba-only. 90-docs as a whole is not** -- 617 .edn remain (business 165,\nlake 77, community-coverage 46, maturity 42, evidence 39, ...), and\n`scripts/fleet-ci/gates/docs-edn-check.cljs` accepts both extensions\n(it globs `*.edn` and `*.kotoba`, because a .kotoba data file is\nS-expressions and cljs.reader already parses it). Writing kotoba-only\nacross 90-docs would put 617 conforming files in violation overnight.\n\nWhat did NOT change: EDN/kotoba is still the sole book of record for the\nADR plane, md is still not a source, the shape is still tx-data, nested\nvalues are still pr-str blobs, and datom query is still the read path.\n\nTwo tools still carry the old assumption and are named rather than fixed\nhere: `scripts/adr-new.cljs` emits `.edn` and a bare numeric id (both\nagainst current rules), and `manifest/docs-edn-only.cljs` still states\n`正本は 90-docs/adr/*.edn` in its header.\n")))
